  "notes": "Chicken pieces skinless, edible yield 70 %. All 125 ml oil stays in the pot (onions, potatoes and chicken are cooked in it and it is layered into the breyani), so all of it is counted. Lentils tinned, drained 240 g. Sanity check: FatSecret ZA chicken biryani 139 kcal / 100 g; UK FSA chicken biryani 646 kcal a serving; Arise chicken biryani with potato 633 kcal. Ours is 980 kcal because a sixth of this pot is a ~730 g plate (rice, chicken, potato, lentils and egg); per 100 g it is ~135 kcal, in line with the published density. The 125 ml oil (~170 kcal a serving) is the biggest single swing."
